(5897144, 858914, 23484, '<td valign="top">I like this. Your shot fits your title well so well. Usually the title fits the shot. Nice job.</td>', 'I like this. Your shot fits your title well so well. Usually the title fits the shot. Nice job.', '2010-03-09 18:41:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897145, 858137, 23484, '<td valign="top">Very well done. I love the texture.</td>', 'Very well done. I love the texture.', '2010-03-09 18:42:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897146, 859022, 23484, '<td valign="top">Very nice capture and the grainy b&amp;w is fantastic.</td>', 'Very nice capture and the grainy b&w is fantastic.', '2010-03-09 18:43:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897148, 859223, 23484, '<td valign="top">Hard to look at. It certainly grabed my attention.</td>', 'Hard to look at. It certainly grabed my attention.', '2010-03-09 18:44:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897149, 859035, 52336, '<td valign="top">Yeah, this is beautiful.  I don''t like it for the obvious allegory, but I like it for the sparseness and the gentle curves.  Even more negative space at top would have made this a real winner for me; if the sky was weighing down on the lightness of the scene, and the white hill was just a little less in view, and the whole thing just pushed down slightly.  I would have been touched by that.  But thanks, this is very pretty.</td>', 'Yeah, this is beautiful.  I don''t like it for the obvious allegory, but I like it for the sparseness and the gentle curves.  Even more negative space at top would have made this a real winner for me; if the sky was weighing down on the lightness of the scene, and the white hill was just a little less in view, and the whole thing just pushed down slightly.  I would have been touched by that.  But thanks, this is very pretty.', '2010-03-09 18:44:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897150, 858240, 23484, '<td valign="top">Very neat. The title is perfect.</td>', 'Very neat. The title is perfect.', '2010-03-09 18:45:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897151, 859146, 23484, '<td valign="top">...but it is still a rose. Nice job.</td>', '...but it is still a rose. Nice job.', '2010-03-09 18:45:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897153, 859113, 52336, '<td valign="top">It''s an interesting scene, but it''s not special.  "Fine art" photos are special, in some way.  They aren''t necessarily "of" something, in my opinion, nor do they necessarily have to be metaphoric.  But they have to be touching.  I don''t feel this image.  I know what it is, but not what you meant by it.</td>', 'It''s an interesting scene, but it''s not special.  "Fine art" photos are special, in some way.  They aren''t necessarily "of" something, in my opinion, nor do they necessarily have to be metaphoric.  But they have to be touching.  I don''t feel this image.  I know what it is, but not what you meant by it.', '2010-03-09 18:45:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897154, 858802, 68769, '<td valign="top">Exceptional, consider it a Roman numeral..</td>', 'Exceptional, consider it a Roman numeral..', '2010-03-09 18:46:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897157, 859169, 23484, '<td valign="top">I like the three separated images (so to speak). The colors are great.</td>', 'I like the three separated images (so to speak). The colors are great.', '2010-03-09 18:46:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897158, 859118, 52336, '<td valign="top">A good capture, a lovely (and super-intelligent) bird, an odd colour choice, and not really "fine art".  It doesn''t work for me beyond interesting comparisons of texture vis-a-vis the wings and needles.  What is going on here?</td>', 'A good capture, a lovely (and super-intelligent) bird, an odd colour choice, and not really "fine art".  It doesn''t work for me beyond interesting comparisons of texture vis-a-vis the wings and needles.  What is going on here?', '2010-03-09 18:47:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897160, 859226, 68769, '<td valign="top">I pity the judges..</td>', 'I pity the judges..', '2010-03-09 18:47:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897162, 859183, 52336, '<td valign="top">It *is* a door, that''s true.  But *why* is it a door?  If you had asked that question with your photograph, if you had made me think of this door, instead of the Lensbaby effect, or the bare tree in the way, or why you decided to photograph this door at all, I would have called this a success.  Instead, I can only call it what it is: a door.</td>', 'It *is* a door, that''s true.  But *why* is it a door?  If you had asked that question with your photograph, if you had made me think of this door, instead of the Lensbaby effect, or the bare tree in the way, or why you decided to photograph this door at all, I would have called this a success.  Instead, I can only call it what it is: a door.', '2010-03-09 18:48:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897165, 858236, 52336, '<td valign="top">A mummy, I assume.  But in my opinion, not fine art.  Although it is compositionally good, and you''ve taken an overall nice photograph with good technicals, I don''t know why you took this photograph at all.  Are you in there somewhere?  Where?  What''s going on?  What does it all mean?  Speak to me, already...</td>', 'A mummy, I assume.  But in my opinion, not fine art.  Although it is compositionally good, and you''ve taken an overall nice photograph with good technicals, I don''t know why you took this photograph at all.  Are you in there somewhere?  Where?  What''s going on?  What does it all mean?  Speak to me, already...', '2010-03-09 18:50:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897169, 858883, 52336, '<td valign="top">A creek bed, it seems.  Abstraction occasionally works as fine art.  This is texturally interesting, but not evocative of anything in particular (it doesn''t touch me, connect with me).  For that reason, I can''t personally label this as "fine art".  I like looking, though.  There are many textural layers that one can see.</td>', 'A creek bed, it seems.  Abstraction occasionally works as fine art.  This is texturally interesting, but not evocative of anything in particular (it doesn''t touch me, connect with me).  For that reason, I can''t personally label this as "fine art".  I like looking, though.  There are many textural layers that one can see.', '2010-03-09 18:52:32.000000', NULL, 1),
