(5897231, 859123, 52336, '<td valign="top">Very aggressively processed, and therefore, for me, not as effective as possible.  It also appears to have been taken in low light, and so the blur and grain -- to be interpreted as elements of "fine art" I suppose -- detract.  Nice angle though, and I''d be interested in the context in which this was taken.</td>', 'Very aggressively processed, and therefore, for me, not as effective as possible.  It also appears to have been taken in low light, and so the blur and grain -- to be interpreted as elements of "fine art" I suppose -- detract.  Nice angle though, and I''d be interested in the context in which this was taken.', '2010-03-09 19:22:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897232, 859206, 52336, '<td valign="top">This is more abstract than artistic.  The two may sometimes coalesce, but this isn''t successful as "fine art", in my view.  Funky though.  Tie-dye-ish.</td>', 'This is more abstract than artistic.  The two may sometimes coalesce, but this isn''t successful as "fine art", in my view.  Funky though.  Tie-dye-ish.', '2010-03-09 19:22:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897241, 858297, 68769, '<td valign="top">Interesting, far from getting it, I will revisit..</td>', 'Interesting, far from getting it, I will revisit..', '2010-03-09 19:29:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897243, 858667, 68769, '<td valign="top">I like your story..</td>', 'I like your story..', '2010-03-09 19:30:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897245, 858813, 52336, '<td valign="top">I''ve been seeing a lot of photos along these lines in this challenge (purposefully odd, weird for the sake of weird).  Sometimes it works.  Sometimes not.  Though interesting, with well done light and an imaginative setup -- complete with a projected X-ray, I guess -- its oddness does not connect with me.  In my view, "fine art" almost always connects with someone, somewhere.  It has *something* to say, to somebody, about the photographer, or the metaphor should there be one, or about photography.  What''s going on here?  I just don''t know.</td>', 'I''ve been seeing a lot of photos along these lines in this challenge (purposefully odd, weird for the sake of weird).  Sometimes it works.  Sometimes not.  Though interesting, with well done light and an imaginative setup -- complete with a projected X-ray, I guess -- its oddness does not connect with me.  In my view, "fine art" almost always connects with someone, somewhere.  It has *something* to say, to somebody, about the photographer, or the metaphor should there be one, or about photography.  What''s going on here?  I just don''t know.', '2010-03-09 19:32:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897247, 859064, 68769, '<td valign="top">Nice work, like the texture.</td>', 'Nice work, like the texture.', '2010-03-09 19:33:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897248, 858967, 52336, '<td valign="top">This really would have worked for me, if it were just a cube, and all duo.  The balance is lovely, the grain, whether imposed or in the scene, perfect, the photograph, but for the colour and the fact that it''s Rubik''s cube, restrained and spare.  It could have been so perfect.  But it isn''t.  Thank you for the rest of it.</td>', 'This really would have worked for me, if it were just a cube, and all duo.  The balance is lovely, the grain, whether imposed or in the scene, perfect, the photograph, but for the colour and the fact that it''s Rubik''s cube, restrained and spare.  It could have been so perfect.  But it isn''t.  Thank you for the rest of it.', '2010-03-09 19:34:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(5897250, 858689, 68769, '<td valign="top">Great colors, feels good.</td>', 'Great colors, feels good.', '2010-03-09 19:34:44.000000', NULL, 1),
