(5902606, 859166, 70265, '<td valign="top">Love what you''ve achieved here through the processing.</td>', 'Love what you''ve achieved here through the processing.', '2010-03-13 14:09:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5902608, 858600, 70265, '<td valign="top">One of my favorites. Love the movement the birds create. PP &amp; border perfect for this. The one dot of color leads your eye into the scene.</td>', 'One of my favorites. Love the movement the birds create. PP & border perfect for this. The one dot of color leads your eye into the scene.', '2010-03-13 14:13:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5902610, 858802, 70265, '<td valign="top">Simple, effective. I would try a square crop &amp; lose the vignette border.</td>', 'Simple, effective. I would try a square crop & lose the vignette border.', '2010-03-13 14:15:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5902633, 859033, 63218, '<td valign="top">I''m not making this up: I had a dream a bout this photo last night. I was painting hot-pink and dayglo-lavender, &amp; lime green on this with an airbrush. Of course I often dream in post-processing terms, but this is a first. "D</td>', 'I''m not making this up: I had a dream a bout this photo last night. I was painting hot-pink and dayglo-lavender, & lime green on this with an airbrush. Of course I often dream in post-processing terms, but this is a first. "D', '2010-03-13 15:08:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(5902634, 858913, 63218, '<td valign="top">This resists all my attempts to understand, explain, or even comment on it, it is so awesomely amazingly brilliant. I looked at it for 10 min. before I saw the 4th lamp. The mirror (I think it is a mirror?) is a stroke of genius. If I could give it 10 twice, I would.</td>', 'This resists all my attempts to understand, explain, or even comment on it, it is so awesomely amazingly brilliant. I looked at it for 10 min. before I saw the 4th lamp. The mirror (I think it is a mirror?) is a stroke of genius. If I could give it 10 twice, I would.', '2010-03-13 15:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5902637, 858654, 64086, '<td valign="top">Very cool. The TV is classic! Everything is spectacular...the emptiness, the outfit, the pose. My only nit pick is the black shadow on the chest from the bottom of the mask. Great Job.</td>', 'Very cool. The TV is classic! Everything is spectacular...the emptiness, the outfit, the pose. My only nit pick is the black shadow on the chest from the bottom of the mask. Great Job.', '2010-03-13 15:18:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5902639, 859023, 39850, '<td valign="top">8 - I like the uniqueness of this.  In photography, I haven''t seen anything similar to this (but I don''t get around much these days).  The simplicity and the lines and the colors and the three figures all work well and there is good balance in the composition, especially with the rise in the distant landscape on the left side with the solitary figure.  The colors, while very muted, work well - if you changed any hues or adjusted the saturation, this must be your personal color wheel choice - a variation would likely have more impact for me, but this is your vision, not mine.</td>', '8 - I like the uniqueness of this.  In photography, I haven''t seen anything similar to this (but I don''t get around much these days).  The simplicity and the lines and the colors and the three figures all work well and there is good balance in the composition, especially with the rise in the distant landscape on the left side with the solitary figure.  The colors, while very muted, work well - if you changed any hues or adjusted the saturation, this must be your personal color wheel choice - a variation would likely have more impact for me, but this is your vision, not mine.', '2010-03-13 15:23:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(5902640, 859212, 39850, '<td valign="top">8 - Well, of course I have been trying to decipher what I''m looking at - I''ll take a small guess that it is some type of ''sink/drain hole'', perhaps partly fabricated by you.  Either way, I like the machine look to it and your title echoes that.  I like the tinted tone and composition, although it seems slightly off balance to my eye.</td>', '8 - Well, of course I have been trying to decipher what I''m looking at - I''ll take a small guess that it is some type of ''sink/drain hole'', perhaps partly fabricated by you.  Either way, I like the machine look to it and your title echoes that.  I like the tinted tone and composition, although it seems slightly off balance to my eye.', '2010-03-13 15:25:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5902641, 858793, 39850, '<td valign="top">8 - I like the scene, the tones, the elements, shapes, lines, light and even the frame - my biggest ''nit-pick'' with this image is the ''ordinariness'' of the woman(?) - oh for a wheelchair or something odd... (but it is your vision/''art'', not mine).</td>', '8 - I like the scene, the tones, the elements, shapes, lines, light and even the frame - my biggest ''nit-pick'' with this image is the ''ordinariness'' of the woman(?) - oh for a wheelchair or something odd... (but it is your vision/''art'', not mine).', '2010-03-13 15:27:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5902643, 859021, 39850, '<td valign="top">8 - I like this, but it seems lacking punch, especially in the water/''background'' - but if that is deliberate, then there ya go.  I think my mind is also unsettled by the lack of symmetry (seemingly) - it is there in the reflection, but the ''realistic perspective'', where the water ripples are, etc - makes my mind think that the angle is wrong, somehow.</td>', '8 - I like this, but it seems lacking punch, especially in the water/''background'' - but if that is deliberate, then there ya go.  I think my mind is also unsettled by the lack of symmetry (seemingly) - it is there in the reflection, but the ''realistic perspective'', where the water ripples are, etc - makes my mind think that the angle is wrong, somehow.', '2010-03-13 15:30:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5902649, 858968, 28427, '<td valign="top">Revisiting this entry and reviewing the score I gave - up with 2 points.<br/>Am I seeing some kind of bubbles there at the left side? I do wonder what I''m looking at.</td>', 'Revisiting this entry and reviewing the score I gave - up with 2 points.Am I seeing some kind of bubbles there at the left side? I do wonder what I''m looking at.', '2010-03-13 15:41:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(5902650, 858824, 28427, '<td valign="top">I don''t think he will mind this persiflage on "The Scream"<br/>Edit: revisiting entry en reviewing score : up with 2 points.</td>', 'I don''t think he will mind this persiflage on "The Scream"Edit: revisiting entry en reviewing score : up with 2 points.', '2010-03-13 15:42:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(5902651, 857780, 39850, '<td valign="top">8 - This is a tricky one for me, as I <i>do</i> really like the image, <i>especially</i> the shrubs/bushes/trees at the fore and the distant colors, mist/haze and light creeping in.  That part of the image, personally, I can perceive more as ''fine art'', but the border detracts and the visible sun and disproportionate mountains (including that their ''shape'' doesn''t add to the image, isn''t ''used''), throws me from the scene and makes this more of a landscape photograph - almost like two images in one.  It just seems unbalanced, in more ways than one.  Despite the urge after writing this, I still can''t take it down to 7 from 8 - I do like it.</td>', '8 - This is a tricky one for me, as I do really like the image, especially the shrubs/bushes/trees at the fore and the distant colors, mist/haze and light creeping in.  That part of the image, personally, I can perceive more as ''fine art'', but the border detracts and the visible sun and disproportionate mountains (including that their ''shape'' doesn''t add to the image, isn''t ''used''), throws me from the scene and makes this more of a landscape photograph - almost like two images in one.  It just seems unbalanced, in more ways than one.  Despite the urge after writing this, I still can''t take it down to 7 from 8 - I do like it.', '2010-03-13 15:42:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5902653, 858282, 28427, '<td valign="top">Revisiting entry and reviewing score: up with 2 points.</td>', 'Revisiting entry and reviewing score: up with 2 points.', '2010-03-13 15:44:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(5902655, 858538, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice, but for me the border detracts from the simplicity, colors and shadow element.</td>', '7 - Nice, but for me the border detracts from the simplicity, colors and shadow element.', '2010-03-13 15:45:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(5902657, 859248, 28427, '<td valign="top">Revisited entry and reviewed score: up with 1 point.</td>', 'Revisited entry and reviewed score: up with 1 point.', '2010-03-13 15:48:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5902658, 858917, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - The b&amp;w works well to pick up on the shadows and shapes.  Your call, of course, but for me - the scene itself is not that ''absurd'' -  maybe if it was a little bunch of them or something else (and no not that) blown up, might make me think, as the viewer, "oh that''s absurd".. Also, because of your title, my mind wants to see some type of theatre scene in the shadows there - puppets, strings, props, something.  I like the concept though, just think there''s more room to explore/create with the idea.</td>', '7 - The b&w works well to pick up on the shadows and shapes.  Your call, of course, but for me - the scene itself is not that ''absurd'' -  maybe if it was a little bunch of them or something else (and no not that) blown up, might make me think, as the viewer, "oh that''s absurd".. Also, because of your title, my mind wants to see some type of theatre scene in the shadows there - puppets, strings, props, something.  I like the concept though, just think there''s more room to explore/create with the idea.', '2010-03-13 15:49:03.000000', NULL, 1),
