(5910284, 859027, 6999, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Ja-9:</b></div><hr/><i> for me this borders on tasteless, I have grown up in an Elderly Care facility and it just screams exploiting....I am overly sensitive to this...sorry </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I think this is an inaccurate reaction - it would scream ''exploitation'' if it weren''t so carefully composed, and indeed so carefully posed. Whilst there is no apparent attempt to ''airbrush'' the image to produce a fake and sentimental kind of acceptability, there is likewise no attempt to show humiliation of the subject; it''s a good honest photo - although of course very carefully organised and lit. <br/> <br/>I''m surprised by the allegations of its being ''extreme'' or the like, also: it worries me that in a world where you can''t move for images of the flesh, the presentation of some that isn''t tanned, made-up, styled, photoshopped and re-touched should be considered difficult. Surely the constant onslaught of the fake should be more worrying?</td>', 'Originally posted by Ja-9: for me this borders on tasteless, I have grown up in an Elderly Care facility and it just screams exploiting....I am overly sensitive to this...sorry   I think this is an inaccurate reaction - it would scream ''exploitation'' if it weren''t so carefully composed, and indeed so carefully posed. Whilst there is no apparent attempt to ''airbrush'' the image to produce a fake and sentimental kind of acceptability, there is likewise no attempt to show humiliation of the subject; it''s a good honest photo - although of course very carefully organised and lit.  I''m surprised by the allegations of its being ''extreme'' or the like, also: it worries me that in a world where you can''t move for images of the flesh, the presentation of some that isn''t tanned, made-up, styled, photoshopped and re-touched should be considered difficult. Surely the constant onslaught of the fake should be more worrying?', '2010-03-19 06:23:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(5910317, 858654, 89230, '<td valign="top">Fantastic. My favorite photo of the challenge. I really like this!</td>', 'Fantastic. My favorite photo of the challenge. I really like this!', '2010-03-19 07:50:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(5910541, 859177, 68504, '<td valign="top">I liked this.  It is almost all composition and texture, allowing the goose to serve up the frisson.  I suspect it would print way better than it looks on the monitor especially at this size, and indeed this is one of the dangers of this venue - I find myself catering to the electronic display rather than thinking about ink and paper.<br/> <br/>The spareness or understatement of your elements says fine art to me.</td>', 'I liked this.  It is almost all composition and texture, allowing the goose to serve up the frisson.  I suspect it would print way better than it looks on the monitor especially at this size, and indeed this is one of the dangers of this venue - I find myself catering to the electronic display rather than thinking about ink and paper. The spareness or understatement of your elements says fine art to me.', '2010-03-19 14:17:12.000000', NULL, 0),
